implementationPlan.description:
RED GUARD TESTS FIRST, following an existing precedent: scripts/tests/local-runner-check.test.mjs ~274 reads ../../.github/workflows/ci.yml and asserts its own file sits on a `run: node --test` line. Add one such test to EACH suite, so removing either file from CI fails that suite wherever it runs.
- scripts/tests/daemon-json-cap.test.mjs: `test('CI runs this suite on Linux and Windows', ...)`.
- scripts/tests/seat-registration.test.mjs: the same.

Each test:
(a) reads ci.yml through `new URL('../../.github/workflows/ci.yml', import.meta.url)` and normalizes CRLF;
(b) finds the step whose `run: node --test ...` line includes ` scripts/tests/<this file>` as a whole token (regex like the precedent's), and asserts it exists;
(c) asserts that the same step's `if:` line, the nearest `if:` between that step's `- name:` and its `run:`, is absent or is exactly `runner.os != 'macOS'`, so Linux always runs it;
(d) asserts the step belongs to the `build-all-platforms:` job: its line index lies after the `  build-all-platforms:` header and before the next top-level job header.
Keep it line-based with no YAML dependency, as the precedent is. Error handling: a missing ci.yml or step fails with an assert message naming the file. Never wrap it in try/skip.

Run `node --test scripts/tests/daemon-json-cap.test.mjs scripts/tests/seat-registration.test.mjs` with MOE_*/CLAUDE* unset. Exactly the two new tests must fail (the file is not in ci.yml yet), and every existing case must stay green. Record the red output. Report both files in complete_step modifiedFiles.
